  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-foundations",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": -340,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "FOUNDATIONS\n\nThese four boards are the contract. Everything else in the product is assembled from them.\n\nRead a value here, and it is the value \u2014 the artboards are drawn at true size, so a 48px control really is 48px on screen.\n\nWhen this becomes packages/ui, these four boards are what the token file has to contain. Nothing in Components or Screens introduces a value that is not on this page."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-components",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": -340,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "COMPONENTS\n\nEvery state is drawn rather than triggered, so nothing that a developer has to build is left undocumented.\n\nBoard 09 is the one to read first. Those four patterns are not style choices \u2014 each one is a constitution principle that only exists if the interface carries it, and each names the rule it comes from."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-screens",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": -340,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "SCREENS\n\nAssembled only from Components, using only Foundations values. If a screen here needed something new, it went back into a component board first.\n\nContent is realistic sample data, not real records. The household, the names and the document ids are invented.\n\nBoards 10 and 15 together cover spec 006: 10 is the paths taken when things go right, 15 is every other state the spec requires. Frame labels cite the acceptance scenario.\n\nBoard 14 is the same system at 1440px: no new components, a rail instead of a tab bar, 40px controls instead of 48."
    }
  ],
